WEBVTT

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:02.960
If your business can't run without

00:00:01.309 --> 00:00:05.120
[music] you for more than a week, you

00:00:02.960 --> 00:00:07.440
don't own a business. You own a job. And

00:00:05.120 --> 00:00:09.120
it's probably paying you a lot less per

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:10.800
hour than you actually think. [music] My

00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:12.719
name is Austin Zach and I've spent the

00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:14.799
last 10 years building companies that do

00:00:12.719 --> 00:00:16.960
over 8 figures in annual revenue. Many

00:00:14.799 --> 00:00:18.560
of which run completely without me for

00:00:16.960 --> 00:00:20.800
months at a time. And that didn't happen

00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:22.480
by me working harder. It happened by me

00:00:20.800 --> 00:00:25.119
looking at my time [music] and at

00:00:22.480 --> 00:00:27.510
leverage and me evaluating if where I

00:00:25.119 --> 00:00:29.199
was spending my time had the highest ROI

00:00:27.510 --> 00:00:31.359
[music] that it could have. Because the

00:00:29.199 --> 00:00:33.440
truth is, hard work alone will only take

00:00:31.359 --> 00:00:35.040
you so far. And in the next 10 minutes,

00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:37.120
I'm going to show you exactly what

00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:39.360
breaks through it when you need it and

00:00:37.120 --> 00:00:41.280
how to implement it so your business can

00:00:39.360 --> 00:00:43.200
finally scale without you being the

00:00:41.280 --> 00:00:45.040
bottleneck. Most entrepreneurs believe

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:47.039
the same lie that if you just work

00:00:45.040 --> 00:00:48.960
harder, you'll eventually win. And

00:00:47.039 --> 00:00:51.039
you're right. For a while, you close

00:00:48.960 --> 00:00:52.960
more deals, revenue climbs, and you tell

00:00:51.039 --> 00:00:54.320
yourself, "This is what it takes." But

00:00:52.960 --> 00:00:55.840
here's the problem. You're not building

00:00:54.320 --> 00:00:57.600
a business that can actually scale

00:00:55.840 --> 00:01:00.480
without you. You're building a business

00:00:57.600 --> 00:01:02.480
that requires you to run that business.

00:01:00.480 --> 00:01:05.280
Every decision has to go through you.

00:01:02.480 --> 00:01:06.960
Every fire requires you to put it out.

00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:09.280
You become the hardest worker in your

00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:11.760
company. And that becomes the biggest

00:01:09.280 --> 00:01:14.080
problem. You can't grow beyond yourself

00:01:11.760 --> 00:01:15.360
if everything requires you to be

00:01:14.080 --> 00:01:17.280
present. Here's how you know if you're

00:01:15.360 --> 00:01:19.119
the bottleneck. Ask yourself this one

00:01:17.280 --> 00:01:21.520
simple question. If you disappeared

00:01:19.119 --> 00:01:23.439
right now for six months, would the

00:01:21.520 --> 00:01:25.200
business continue to scale or would it

00:01:23.439 --> 00:01:27.280
totally fall apart? And if the answer is

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:29.439
it falls apart, then you don't own a

00:01:27.280 --> 00:01:31.200
business. You are the business. And

00:01:29.439 --> 00:01:33.119
here's why that's a problem. You can put

00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:35.040
the right person in the wrong seat and

00:01:33.119 --> 00:01:37.040
it won't work. And you can put the wrong

00:01:35.040 --> 00:01:38.880
person in the right seat and it won't

00:01:37.040 --> 00:01:40.720
work. And sometimes the seat doesn't

00:01:38.880 --> 00:01:42.560
even need to exist. That's ultimately

00:01:40.720 --> 00:01:44.960
how companies get bloated. But if you

00:01:42.560 --> 00:01:46.640
try to sit in all of the seats yourself,

00:01:44.960 --> 00:01:48.479
you're guaranteed to cap out. Let me

00:01:46.640 --> 00:01:50.079
give you an example from my wholesaling

00:01:48.479 --> 00:01:51.600
company. I was sitting in every seat at

00:01:50.079 --> 00:01:54.159
one point. I was sitting in sales,

00:01:51.600 --> 00:01:56.000
marketing, operations, you name it. I

00:01:54.159 --> 00:01:58.159
was literally going to the bank multiple

00:01:56.000 --> 00:01:59.920
times a day because I always wanted to

00:01:58.159 --> 00:02:01.439
make sure that we had enough money in

00:01:59.920 --> 00:02:03.200
our checking account to cover our

00:02:01.439 --> 00:02:05.040
expenses the next day. So, if we got a

00:02:03.200 --> 00:02:06.960
check at noon, I went to the bank at

00:02:05.040 --> 00:02:08.239
noon. If we got another check at 3:00 in

00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:09.920
the afternoon, I would go to the bank

00:02:08.239 --> 00:02:11.599
again. Like, I was literally doing

00:02:09.920 --> 00:02:13.840
everything. And you know what happened?

00:02:11.599 --> 00:02:15.360
I got to a point where I hated my life.

00:02:13.840 --> 00:02:17.280
I would wake up every morning with the

00:02:15.360 --> 00:02:19.200
weight on my shoulders of this machine

00:02:17.280 --> 00:02:20.879
that I built. But the problem was is

00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:22.879
that I couldn't turn the machine off.

00:02:20.879 --> 00:02:24.640
Like there was no off button. But at the

00:02:22.879 --> 00:02:26.239
same time, it wouldn't run without me.

00:02:24.640 --> 00:02:27.680
Some of my sales guys were making more

00:02:26.239 --> 00:02:29.599
money than me. I didn't have any

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:31.120
freedom. And I literally felt like I was

00:02:29.599 --> 00:02:33.200
trapped. And that's when I realized I

00:02:31.120 --> 00:02:34.800
had two choices. I could keep doing the

00:02:33.200 --> 00:02:37.280
same thing that I was doing and keep

00:02:34.800 --> 00:02:39.120
getting the same result. Or I could go

00:02:37.280 --> 00:02:40.959
ahead and get uncomfortable. I could do

00:02:39.120 --> 00:02:42.640
things that were totally outside of my

00:02:40.959 --> 00:02:44.480
comfort zone that I had never done

00:02:42.640 --> 00:02:46.400
before. I could hire people. I could

00:02:44.480 --> 00:02:48.080
delegate. I could try to figure out how

00:02:46.400 --> 00:02:50.480
to put the right people in the right

00:02:48.080 --> 00:02:52.239
seat and ultimately start to take a

00:02:50.480 --> 00:02:53.760
backseat. So, I started to hire people

00:02:52.239 --> 00:02:56.319
and bring them on. And you know what

00:02:53.760 --> 00:02:58.560
happened? I got better. And in 90 days,

00:02:56.319 --> 00:03:00.400
things started to change drastically. I

00:02:58.560 --> 00:03:02.879
forced myself to learn that nobody can

00:03:00.400 --> 00:03:04.800
do everything at scale, not all at once.

00:03:02.879 --> 00:03:06.959
And I realized that all of the things

00:03:04.800 --> 00:03:09.040
that I was doing at half capacity

00:03:06.959 --> 00:03:10.959
because I was stretched way too thin,

00:03:09.040 --> 00:03:12.720
the people that I brought in and hired

00:03:10.959 --> 00:03:14.959
were able to do them even better than

00:03:12.720 --> 00:03:16.400
me. and they were able to do them fast.

00:03:14.959 --> 00:03:18.480
It means trusting people with your

00:03:16.400 --> 00:03:20.560
vision and understanding and accepting

00:03:18.480 --> 00:03:22.800
that they might actually do things that

00:03:20.560 --> 00:03:24.800
are different than you envisioned. And

00:03:22.800 --> 00:03:26.080
it just might be better than how you

00:03:24.800 --> 00:03:28.560
would have done it. But I'm telling you

00:03:26.080 --> 00:03:30.319
right now, it is the only way to scale

00:03:28.560 --> 00:03:32.319
if you're an entrepreneur. So, here's

00:03:30.319 --> 00:03:35.120
what actually scales a business. The

00:03:32.319 --> 00:03:37.440
right people in the right seat. Not just

00:03:35.120 --> 00:03:39.200
hard workers, not just order takers,

00:03:37.440 --> 00:03:41.440
people who are legitimately better than

00:03:39.200 --> 00:03:43.360
you at specific things. So if you've

00:03:41.440 --> 00:03:45.360
read traction or rocket fuel then you

00:03:43.360 --> 00:03:47.360
know that every business needs this

00:03:45.360 --> 00:03:49.200
framework. You need a visionary and you

00:03:47.360 --> 00:03:51.599
need an integrator. The visionary is the

00:03:49.200 --> 00:03:54.080
big picture person. Think ideas,

00:03:51.599 --> 00:03:56.239
strategy, brand. Then the integrator

00:03:54.080 --> 00:03:59.200
comes in and they execute on that. Think

00:03:56.239 --> 00:04:01.360
operations, systems, processes. And most

00:03:59.200 --> 00:04:03.040
entrepreneurs try to do both and they're

00:04:01.360 --> 00:04:04.799
terrible at at least one of them. But

00:04:03.040 --> 00:04:07.439
here's what most people miss. You need

00:04:04.799 --> 00:04:09.360
to find who's not hows. So there are

00:04:07.439 --> 00:04:12.000
really two types of who's. So you have

00:04:09.360 --> 00:04:13.920
hired who's people that you pay to do a

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:15.760
specific job. They do one thing at a

00:04:13.920 --> 00:04:17.280
really high level and they actually end

00:04:15.760 --> 00:04:18.880
up filling gaps that you didn't even

00:04:17.280 --> 00:04:20.639
know you had. And then you have found

00:04:18.880 --> 00:04:22.400
who's and these are people like mentors

00:04:20.639 --> 00:04:24.479
and adviserss. And these are people that

00:04:22.400 --> 00:04:26.240
you can typically get to give you advice

00:04:24.479 --> 00:04:28.160
for free because they've already been

00:04:26.240 --> 00:04:30.320
where you're at. And they're able to

00:04:28.160 --> 00:04:32.479
shave years off of your learning curve

00:04:30.320 --> 00:04:34.240
and ultimately save you hundreds of

00:04:32.479 --> 00:04:36.320
thousands and maybe even millions of

00:04:34.240 --> 00:04:38.160
dollars. And here's why hired who's are

00:04:36.320 --> 00:04:39.840
such a valuable asset to your company.

00:04:38.160 --> 00:04:41.280
They're typically not entrepreneurs.

00:04:39.840 --> 00:04:42.880
They don't want the risk. They don't

00:04:41.280 --> 00:04:44.880
want to build their own puzzle from

00:04:42.880 --> 00:04:46.880
scratch. They want to find a way to fit

00:04:44.880 --> 00:04:48.560
into yours and make good money doing it.

00:04:46.880 --> 00:04:49.919
They want the high pay and maybe a

00:04:48.560 --> 00:04:52.080
little bit of equity, but they don't

00:04:49.919 --> 00:04:54.479
want to bear the weight of the entire

00:04:52.080 --> 00:04:56.400
business on their back like you or me.

00:04:54.479 --> 00:04:58.160
They don't want the sleepless nights.

00:04:56.400 --> 00:05:00.320
And that is not a weakness. That is

00:04:58.160 --> 00:05:02.479
exactly what makes them a perfect fit

00:05:00.320 --> 00:05:03.840
for your company. So, what I did was I

00:05:02.479 --> 00:05:05.600
went ahead and I brought on multiple

00:05:03.840 --> 00:05:07.600
partners and they were all integrators

00:05:05.600 --> 00:05:09.280
cuz I'm the visionary. And a lot of my

00:05:07.600 --> 00:05:11.520
integrator partners, they helped build

00:05:09.280 --> 00:05:13.680
out the systems, the processes, all the

00:05:11.520 --> 00:05:16.080
SOPs for each individual company. And

00:05:13.680 --> 00:05:18.240
then making sure that those SOPs got

00:05:16.080 --> 00:05:20.000
executed on. Some of my other partners

00:05:18.240 --> 00:05:22.080
went ahead and they managed people. They

00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:24.080
managed the culture. They were overall

00:05:22.080 --> 00:05:26.080
great managers. They filled the seats

00:05:24.080 --> 00:05:27.919
that I had no business being in and they

00:05:26.080 --> 00:05:29.680
were way better at it. And so I got the

00:05:27.919 --> 00:05:31.680
hell out of the way. And that is really

00:05:29.680 --> 00:05:33.039
when my businesses started to scale.

00:05:31.680 --> 00:05:35.280
Now, a question you might be wondering

00:05:33.039 --> 00:05:36.960
is, well, do you need partners or do you

00:05:35.280 --> 00:05:38.639
need great employees? So, if you have

00:05:36.960 --> 00:05:40.479
capital, you want to hire the best

00:05:38.639 --> 00:05:42.160
talent in the world. That is my number

00:05:40.479 --> 00:05:44.240
one piece of advice to you. Think about

00:05:42.160 --> 00:05:47.039
Meta for a minute. They're offering a

00:05:44.240 --> 00:05:49.759
hundred million signup bonus just to

00:05:47.039 --> 00:05:51.520
join Meta in the AI race. And Google is

00:05:49.759 --> 00:05:53.199
doing the exact same. And if you don't

00:05:51.520 --> 00:05:54.560
have unlimited capital, then a lot of

00:05:53.199 --> 00:05:56.479
times you'll want to consider bringing

00:05:54.560 --> 00:05:58.000
on a potential partner. A lot of times

00:05:56.479 --> 00:05:59.520
you can get them for free. And if you

00:05:58.000 --> 00:06:01.120
can sell them the dream and you can get

00:05:59.520 --> 00:06:03.840
them to buy into the vision, you can

00:06:01.120 --> 00:06:05.759
typically get a partner that maybe would

00:06:03.840 --> 00:06:07.680
have commanded a couple hundred thousand

00:06:05.759 --> 00:06:09.759
a year salary, but you can get them at

00:06:07.680 --> 00:06:11.680
least initially for free because they're

00:06:09.759 --> 00:06:13.759
willing to delay the gratification of

00:06:11.680 --> 00:06:15.759
getting their paycheck until the company

00:06:13.759 --> 00:06:17.440
actually succeeds. And that really is

00:06:15.759 --> 00:06:19.520
the power of equity and ownership.

00:06:17.440 --> 00:06:21.680
They're betting on the upside, not just

00:06:19.520 --> 00:06:23.360
the initial salary. Now, let me tell you

00:06:21.680 --> 00:06:25.039
what most people get completely wrong

00:06:23.360 --> 00:06:26.400
about this. They think that if you bring

00:06:25.039 --> 00:06:28.160
in the right people and you put them in

00:06:26.400 --> 00:06:29.680
the right seat that you're done, the

00:06:28.160 --> 00:06:31.280
business will just infinitely scale

00:06:29.680 --> 00:06:33.520
forever and you can just sit on the

00:06:31.280 --> 00:06:35.280
beach and drink mojitos and do nothing.

00:06:33.520 --> 00:06:37.199
And that is just not a reality. You

00:06:35.280 --> 00:06:38.720
know, for me, I still wake up at 4:30 in

00:06:37.199 --> 00:06:40.639
the morning every day because I love to.

00:06:38.720 --> 00:06:42.319
I go to the gym, I work out, I have my

00:06:40.639 --> 00:06:44.400
morning routine. Then I come to the

00:06:42.319 --> 00:06:46.800
office at just about the same time every

00:06:44.400 --> 00:06:48.960
day. I have meetings. I oversee multiple

00:06:46.800 --> 00:06:51.600
different companies. I put out any major

00:06:48.960 --> 00:06:53.840
fires on a day-to-day basis. And I solve

00:06:51.600 --> 00:06:55.840
big strategic problems. I leave around

00:06:53.840 --> 00:06:57.600
5:30 at night. I go home. I have dinner

00:06:55.840 --> 00:06:59.039
with my wife. I try to be present. And

00:06:57.600 --> 00:07:01.680
then I go to sleep. And the difference

00:06:59.039 --> 00:07:03.280
is I'm not grinding in the trenches in

00:07:01.680 --> 00:07:05.039
the dayto-day anymore. So, let me give

00:07:03.280 --> 00:07:07.199
you an example of what the fires look

00:07:05.039 --> 00:07:08.880
like for me today versus what they used

00:07:07.199 --> 00:07:10.080
to look like. Before, when a deal fell

00:07:08.880 --> 00:07:11.520
apart in one of my real estate

00:07:10.080 --> 00:07:13.919
companies, I knew about every little

00:07:11.520 --> 00:07:15.680
detail. I knew if an inspection report

00:07:13.919 --> 00:07:17.360
came back or an appraisal or something

00:07:15.680 --> 00:07:18.960
weird was happening with a buyer, with

00:07:17.360 --> 00:07:20.800
the seller. And today, when a deal falls

00:07:18.960 --> 00:07:22.639
apart, I hardly even know about it. I

00:07:20.800 --> 00:07:24.400
get updated in one meeting a week on

00:07:22.639 --> 00:07:26.639
each individual company that we run and

00:07:24.400 --> 00:07:28.560
I get updated with bulk information and

00:07:26.639 --> 00:07:30.160
I only make decisions or give my opinion

00:07:28.560 --> 00:07:32.000
on things that really matter. And the

00:07:30.160 --> 00:07:34.000
hard part sometimes is that there are

00:07:32.000 --> 00:07:36.160
certain problems in my company where I

00:07:34.000 --> 00:07:38.240
know the answer. I could easily jump in.

00:07:36.160 --> 00:07:39.919
I could easily solve the problem. But at

00:07:38.240 --> 00:07:42.000
the level that I'm at now and trying to

00:07:39.919 --> 00:07:44.240
go where we're trying to go, that isn't

00:07:42.000 --> 00:07:46.400
always the best solution. Sometimes the

00:07:44.240 --> 00:07:48.479
best solution is to do nothing and let

00:07:46.400 --> 00:07:50.560
my team organically get better and

00:07:48.479 --> 00:07:52.560
organically figure it out themselves.

00:07:50.560 --> 00:07:54.479
So, can my businesses run right now if

00:07:52.560 --> 00:07:56.000
I'm gone for a week? Absolutely. Could

00:07:54.479 --> 00:07:57.680
they run for 6 months without me

00:07:56.000 --> 00:07:59.280
involved? Yes, they could. And here's

00:07:57.680 --> 00:08:01.759
what nobody talks about. The pressure

00:07:59.280 --> 00:08:03.599
never goes away. It just changes. Before

00:08:01.759 --> 00:08:05.680
the fear was, am I working hard enough

00:08:03.599 --> 00:08:07.280
or am I closing enough deals? And now

00:08:05.680 --> 00:08:08.879
the fear is a little bit different. A

00:08:07.280 --> 00:08:10.400
lot of it is, you know, am I working on

00:08:08.879 --> 00:08:13.039
the highest level thing that I could be

00:08:10.400 --> 00:08:15.759
working on? is what I'm doing the most

00:08:13.039 --> 00:08:17.360
valuable ROI on my time. The pressure is

00:08:15.759 --> 00:08:19.680
just a little bit heavier because now

00:08:17.360 --> 00:08:22.560
it's not just about me. It's about every

00:08:19.680 --> 00:08:24.319
single person that bet on my vision. But

00:08:22.560 --> 00:08:26.160
I always have to remind myself that the

00:08:24.319 --> 00:08:27.680
problems that I have today are the best

00:08:26.160 --> 00:08:29.199
problems that I could have. Their

00:08:27.680 --> 00:08:31.199
strategic problems, their growth

00:08:29.199 --> 00:08:32.399
problems, their scale problems. I

00:08:31.199 --> 00:08:34.000
wouldn't trade it for the world. So

00:08:32.399 --> 00:08:36.640
here's what you need to understand. Hard

00:08:34.000 --> 00:08:38.399
work is the entry fee, not the strategy.

00:08:36.640 --> 00:08:39.839
You need it to get into the game, but if

00:08:38.399 --> 00:08:41.360
that's your only play, you're going to

00:08:39.839 --> 00:08:44.080
cap out. you're going to end up building

00:08:41.360 --> 00:08:45.680
something that needs you 24/7 to

00:08:44.080 --> 00:08:47.360
operate. And at the end of the day, that

00:08:45.680 --> 00:08:49.120
just isn't a business. That's a really

00:08:47.360 --> 00:08:51.040
highpaying job. Freedom doesn't mean

00:08:49.120 --> 00:08:52.720
that you stop working. It means that you

00:08:51.040 --> 00:08:55.519
stop being the bottleneck. You have to

00:08:52.720 --> 00:08:57.680
focus on big picture strategy, hiring,

00:08:55.519 --> 00:08:59.519
firing, the big fires that nobody else

00:08:57.680 --> 00:09:01.360
in the world can put out. And you have

00:08:59.519 --> 00:09:03.279
to believe that other people are going

00:09:01.360 --> 00:09:05.600
to do everything else better than you

00:09:03.279 --> 00:09:07.839
will. Success really trades one pressure

00:09:05.600 --> 00:09:09.920
for another. The question goes from am I

00:09:07.839 --> 00:09:11.760
working hard enough to am I making the

00:09:09.920 --> 00:09:13.440
right decisions that move the company

00:09:11.760 --> 00:09:15.279
forward. The second pressure is a lot

00:09:13.440 --> 00:09:17.360
heavier because you have an entire team

00:09:15.279 --> 00:09:19.279
most likely at that point and all these

00:09:17.360 --> 00:09:20.720
people are people who bet on you and

00:09:19.279 --> 00:09:22.160
your vision. But I'm telling you right

00:09:20.720 --> 00:09:23.760
now that those are problems that are

00:09:22.160 --> 00:09:25.360
worth having and I wouldn't trade it for

00:09:23.760 --> 00:09:28.240
the world. The version of me that slept

00:09:25.360 --> 00:09:30.320
on a futon and worked for 12, 14, 16

00:09:28.240 --> 00:09:32.320
